WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:19.015
It was the last week in August when Mr. Irving and Miss Lavender had their wedding in the garden at Miss Lavender's home.

2
00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:24.059
As they said their vows, gentle rays of sunlight shone down upon them.

3
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:30.616
Paul Irving watched the ceremony happily, looking forward to having a mother once again.

4
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:36.212
After Mr. Irving and Miss Lavender had left for their honeymoon and all the wedding guests had gone,

5
00:00:36.213 --> 00:00:40.324
Anne stayed behind to tidy up Miss Lavender's house.

6
00:00:40.325 --> 00:00:44.388
She was staring out the kitchen window when Gilbert came to help her.

7
00:00:44.389 --> 00:00:48.530
"What are you thinking of, Anne?" Gilbert asked.

8
00:00:48.531 --> 00:00:53.371
"Of Miss Lavender and Mr. Irving," answered Anne dreamily.

9
00:00:53.372 --> 00:00:56.914
"Isn't it beautiful to think how everything has turned out . . .

10
00:00:56.915 --> 00:01:03.448
how they have come together again after all those years of separation and misunderstanding?"

11
00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:09.619
"Yes, it is beautiful," said Gilbert. He looked steadily at Anne.

12
00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:14.344
"But wouldn't it have been more beautiful, Anne, if there had been no separation or misunderstanding—

13
00:01:14.345 --> 00:01:17.576
if they had come hand-in-hand all the way through life?"

14
00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:24.515
For a moment, Anne's heart fluttered, and for the first time, her eyes faltered under Gilbert's gaze.

15
00:01:24.516 --> 00:01:27.934
It was a strange feeling, and she blushed.

16
00:01:27.935 --> 00:01:31.968
When Anne arrived home, Marilla had some sad news.

17
00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:38.714
"Mr. Lynde has died," she said. "He died quietly, in his sleep."

18
00:01:38.715 --> 00:01:45.328
Thomas Lynde had been sick for a long time, and Mrs. Lynde had taken care of him for many years.

19
00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:51.813
Marilla went to comfort Mrs. Lynde and came back to Green Gables the next morning.

20
00:01:51.814 --> 00:02:00.087
Marilla sat down with Anne, who was eating breakfast, and nervously said, "I suppose Gilbert Blythe is going to college in the fall.

21
00:02:00.088 --> 00:02:02.723
Would you like to go to college too?"

22
00:02:02.724 --> 00:02:09.147
Anne looked up, astonished. "Of course, Marilla, but it's not possible!

23
00:02:09.148 --> 00:02:15.464
I know your eyes are better now, but the twins—they need so much looking after."

24
00:02:15.465 --> 00:02:20.471
"Well, I've always felt that you should go to college," said Marilla.

25
00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:29.438
"You've saved enough from your teaching job for one year at Redmond College, and perhaps you could win a scholarship to pay for the other years.

26
00:02:29.439 --> 00:02:36.018
Besides, I wouldn't be alone with the twins. That's what I want to discuss."

27
00:02:36.019 --> 00:02:41.507
Marilla continued, "I had a long talk with Mrs. Lynde last night.

28
00:02:41.508 --> 00:02:45.708
She has to sell her farm, but she doesn't want to leave Avonlea.

29
00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:52.714
So I suggested she move to Green Gables. How do you feel about that?"

30
00:02:52.715 --> 00:02:55.946
"Well, that's your decision, Marilla," said Anne.

31
00:02:55.947 --> 00:03:01.015
"Mrs. Lynde is a good woman and a kind neighbor, but . . ."

32
00:03:01.016 --> 00:03:05.274
"But she's got her faults?" Marilla finished, smiling.

33
00:03:05.275 --> 00:03:11.488
"Well, she does, of course. But if she left Avonlea, I'd miss her terribly.

34
00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:14.594
She's the only close friend I have here.

35
00:03:14.595 --> 00:03:25.155
Mrs. Lynde and I have never had a fight, though we almost did when she met you for the first time, Anne. Do you remember?"

36
00:03:25.156 --> 00:03:30.492
"Yes, I do. I hated her then!" Anne said.

37
00:03:30.493 --> 00:03:35.306
"Well, you were so different from other children, Anne," said Marilla.

38
00:03:35.307 --> 00:03:41.058
"I didn't know how to manage you at first! My brother, Matthew, understood you better."

39
00:03:41.059 --> 00:03:48.139
"Matthew understood everything," said Anne softly, the way she always spoke of him.

40
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:53.819
That night Anne thought long and hard about whether to stop teaching and go to college.

41
00:03:53.820 --> 00:04:02.074
She loved every one of her pupils, even the naughty ones, but the idea of college—of learning more—excited her.

42
00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:11.139
The next day Anne resigned. Meanwhile Mrs. Lynde gratefully accepted Marilla's offer to move into Green Gables.

43
00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:17.932
Gilbert Blythe was probably the only person who was happy to hear the news that Anne was going to college.

44
00:04:17.933 --> 00:04:23.603
Her students looked upon it as a catastrophe. Barbara Shaw cried all night.

45
00:04:23.604 --> 00:04:27.052
Anthony Pye picked a fight because he was so upset.

46
00:04:27.053 --> 00:04:33.596
And Paul Irving defiantly told his father he wouldn't eat any breakfast for a week.

47
00:04:33.597 --> 00:04:39.865
Diana was sad too. "It will be horribly lonely here," she moaned.

48
00:04:39.866 --> 00:04:43.518
"You'll have Fred," Anne teased her, giggling.

49
00:04:43.519 --> 00:04:48.113
"It's all right for you to be happy, Anne," Diana said.

50
00:04:48.114 --> 00:04:53.822
"You're going to college, and you'll have fun and make heaps of lovely new friends."

51
00:04:53.823 --> 00:05:01.869
"I hope I shall make new friends," said Anne thoughtfully. "New friends make life very interesting.

52
00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:08.163
But no matter how many new friends I make, they'll never be as special to me as the old ones.

53
00:05:08.164 --> 00:05:15.007
Especially a certain girl with black eyes and dimples. Can you guess who she is, Diana?"

54
00:05:15.008 --> 00:05:16.689
Diana cheered up.

55
00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:21.304
Anne smiled at her and said, "Do you remember that evening we first met?

56
00:05:21.305 --> 00:05:25.266
We were in your garden and promised eternal friendship.

57
00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:30.487
We've kept that oath, I think. I shall never forget that day.

58
00:05:30.488 --> 00:05:37.219
All through my early childhood, nobody cared for me or wanted to be friends with me.

59
00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:42.263
But when I came to Green Gables, everything changed.

60
00:05:42.264 --> 00:05:45.834
Thank you for your friendship and love, Diana."

61
00:05:45.835 --> 00:06:06.647
Anne and Diana hugged tightly. No matter where Anne went, they were true friends who would remain in each other's hearts always.
